en task.\n\nSummarizing the arXiv papers, none directly match the query \"echo state networks for anomaly detection.\" The closest matches are about graph neural networks and tabular data anomaly detection, not ESNs. \n\nFinal summary: ESNs are used for time-series data processing, with a fixed, randomly connected reservoir layer. They are not commonly used for anomaly detection as per the arXiv search.","role":"assistant"},"model":"qwen2.5:7b","prompt_eval_count":1060,"prompt_eval_duration":45583000,"total_duration":2381039800}}